{"kind":"request","text":"Design review, Draft 5: durability level declared by each scope, and the journal archive in Git. notes/2026-10-09-shared-language-volatile-acts.md at head 2fe8e30d (branch planner/journal-archive-design; parent 6d0ce3c7, Draft 4, on main 70729eac; request 0d72a50b, promise fae322e0). Reporting artifact: the note. Draft 5 answers the two P2s of report f4066bc5. P2, the frozen Mark (15.5): the row names its dependencies and holds no bytes; a rebuild after a restart, a lost reply or a resend reads exactly the entries the manifest names by position from the scope's own journal and exactly the retained inputs it names by kind, domain and digest from the retained store, both immutable for what an entry names (an entry is never rewritten or removed below the head; the retained store keeps an archived kind while an entry names it; texts are never in the set); a rebuild never enumerates current state, so a turn after Mark cannot change it; a named dependency that cannot be read stops the pass as missing-input with the kind, domain and digest reported and nothing substituted; a rebuild that differs stops as rebuild-mismatch; the objects are not persisted because the row and the immutable dependencies make them again; A3 witnesses a reset after Mark before any object reached the host, a later turn retaining a new input, and the identical commit rebuilt with the store instrumented to refuse any read the manifest does not name, plus missing-input on an unreadable dependency. P2, the dependency closure (15.3): the inventory is the replay's own, each #retained and source.retained call of packages/replay/src/verify.ts at main 70729eac, listed by input variant: the declaration the genesis seed names and declarations followed to closure (kind definition), foreign entries cited by uses (entry), rule inputs of prepared (rule), for an act the staged-refs snapshot, the value or declaration each field's place names and the values its recorded observations name (snapshot, value, definition), for a timed input the rule inputs, for an outcome the values its evidence names under its owner declaration and its observations' values (value), nothing further for delivery and checkpoint, and texts never; omissions by kind, domain and digest; A1 fails when a retained read of the verifier is not covered by the table; A2 replays, from the clone alone with no service and no anchor, a scope whose only entry is a declared genesis and a scope whose pass first introduces an outcome-evidence value. The build-time witnesses the report named are recorded as owed, not decided: J9 (overlong legal domain stops without truncation or silent omission; clone integrity and continuity before prefix membership; J2 disclosures before export) and L7 (a locator validates only through an authorized establishing entry; host read admission counts the pre-G bootstrap reads and the membership and watch reads in one budget). Everything credited in f4066bc5 is unchanged: the acyclic seed, the receipt at its own position, the ref encoding and object-store paths, the pinned levels, the withdrawn no-delay claim. Design only; no runtime adoption, no tests, gate or probes. Exact-head review with the three conclusions.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2fbaf52e375c9e6a093761da875e9ec816e9ea9e","branch":"planner/journal-archive-design","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of 2fe8e30d…1878938 with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming git:sha1…6e9ea9e first and resting on all 1 artifacts.","head":"2fe8e30db302fd2cfbb615475ccdddcf11878938","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}